       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       iiccoonnttooppbbmm  was  obsoleted  by  ssuunniiccoonnttooppnnmm(1),  introduced with Netpbm
       10.53 (December 2010).  ssuunniiccoonnttooppnnmm is backward compatible with  iiccoonn‐‐
       ttooppbbmm, plus adds additional functions, including the ability to convert
       a Depth=8 Sun icon, producing a PGM image.

       Starting in Release 10.53, iiccoonnttooppbbmm is just an alias for ssuunniiccoonnttooppnnmm.

       The point of the name change is that there are many kinds of  icons  in
       the  world  besides  Sun icons, and in 2010, the Sun variety isn't even
       common.

       In releases before 10.53, you can use  the  ssuunniiccoonnttooppnnmm  documentation
       for  iiccoonnttooppbbmm,  as  long as you recognize that any change the ssuunniiccoonn‐‐
       ttooppnnmm manual says happened in or after Netpbm 10.53  doesn't  apply  to
       iiccoonnttooppbbmm.

